WEBVTT

00:00:09,140 --> 00:00:14,020
I've read two different articles about avocados, one saying they're histamine activators and

00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:19,700
another saying to eat them as a low histamine food. What do you think? It goes back to our

00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:25,300
histamine question and this we get a lot because this not so fairly on avocados but if you look at

00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:31,780
you google low histamine foods on the internet and you're going to get different lists and the

00:00:31,780 --> 00:00:37,620
reason is is because if we brought foods to a laboratory to test them for histamine levels, it depends

00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:45,620
on how old the foods are that are that we're testing that is going to be that will coordinate to

00:00:45,620 --> 00:00:51,140
the level of histamines we find in them. So if our avocados are overly ripe to probably

00:00:51,140 --> 00:00:59,380
going to have more histamines in it than avocados that are less ripe. I guess we could probably see

00:00:59,380 --> 00:01:04,020
that with every food. So the older the food is the more histamines that are going to be in it,

00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:09,060
that's why the lists are going to be different. So again I would say eat them with balance,

00:01:09,060 --> 00:01:12,500
eat them with balance, eat them with balance, eat them with other foods, eat them with foods,

00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:14,500
other things. So

